    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d125">

                <pb facs="0194" n="174" xml:id="pg174"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">690B.9321/11–2353: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 125<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of
                            State to the Embassy in the Republic of
                            China</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d125-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >secret<lb/>priority</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1953-11-25T19:01:00-05:00">November 25, 1953—7:01
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>473. Considerations advanced Bangkok’s 1033<anchor n="2" xml:id="d125-f2"/> and
                    Rangoon’s 504<anchor n="3" xml:id="d125-f3"/> were included in forceful
                    presentation US views to Ambassador Koo by Robertson 24th. After reviewing
                    apparently deliberate delays and noncompliance with evacuation agreement on part
                    Jungle Generals, Robertson pointed out probable serious consequences to Chinese
                    Government position renewed Burmese complaint UN
                    and mentioned that non-surrender arms would indicate bad faith Chinese
                    Government.</p>
                <p>Koo agreed send urgent telegrams President Chiang and Foreign Minister Yeh
                    expressing US concern in strongest terms. Substance Robertson/Koo conversation
                    summarized in <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> delivered Chinese
                    Embassy late 24th.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d125-f4"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dulles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
